      "message": "If this stays (see my comment on the commit message), I\u0027m worried it no longer applies on aosp/4368056 PS17. There, as Will asked, `validate_page_before_insert()` and `insert_page_into_pte_locked()` are `static` again, declared `static` in a new `mm/p3s/memory.h` that only `mm/memory.c` includes, and `vma_insert_page_slices()` moved there from `mm/p3s/pgtable.h`.\n\nSo `vma_insert_page_slice()` would move next to it, with the new parameter in that `static` declaration and in the `vma_insert_page_slices()` call. It can\u0027t stay in `mm/p3s/pgtable.h`, which `mm/internal.h` pulls into all of `mm/`.\n\nCould the slice add also stay a one-line hook? This open-codes `vma_pte_add_slice()` from aosp/4368054. A variant next to it in `mm/p3s/pgtable.h` that takes the slice index, which `vma_pte_add_slice()` then calls with `vma_slice_offset(vma, addr)`, would leave:\n\n```\n\tpteval \u003d vma_pte_add_slice_idx(vma, pteval, slice_idx);\n```",
