      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it stays, would you mind moving the body and kernel-doc of `vm_insert_page_slice()` into `vma_insert_page_slice()` in `mm/p3s/memory.h`? It can call the `static` helpers declared there, and `mm/memory.c` would only keep the entry point that `mm/vmalloc.c` and `mm/p3s.c` need:\n\n```\nint vm_insert_page_slice(struct vm_area_struct *vma, unsigned long addr,\n\t\t\t struct page *page, unsigned int slice_idx)\n{\n\treturn vma_insert_page_slice(vma, addr, page, slice_idx);\n}\n```\n\nThe helper could set `VM_MIXEDMAP` itself, with a `WARN_ON_ONCE()` for `VM_PFNMAP` instead of the two `BUG_ON()`s. Then `vm_insert_page()` and `vm_insert_pages()` keep upstream\u0027s code and `prepare_vm_insert_page()` isn\u0027t needed. That goes back on the shared helper I asked for on PS7, sorry about that.\n\nThe prototype could then move from `include/linux/mm.h` to `mm/p3s/pgtable.h`, since only `mm/` calls it and it isn\u0027t exported.",
